From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hotty Agent <hotty@neuroplast.io>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 15:23:18 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 46/46] hottyterm: a program's pointer shape waits while a
 surface is hovered
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A motion over a hotty surface is the surface's and never reaches the
program, so the program's idea of the pointer is the last cell it saw
before the surface. A program that sets the pointer's shape per cell
(OSC 22) sends its change one of its frames after the motion. When the
pointer crosses into a surface within that frame, the change for the
cell it left arrived while the surface was hovered, and
Surface.handleMessage showed it at once, over the surface's CSS cursor.
Hotty.shapeChange then showed the surface's shape again only once that
shape changed, or the pointer left the surface.

While a surface is hovered, .set_mouse_shape now shows nothing: the
stream handler has already kept the shape in terminal.mouse_shape, and
shapeChange shows it when the pointer leaves the surface (SPEC §9: over
a surface, the pointer is its document's).
---
 src/Surface.zig      |  3 +++
 src/termio/hotty.zig | 11 +++++++++++
 2 files changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/Surface.zig b/src/Surface.zig
index 31b68a50f..cdb7fdf9a 100644
--- a/src/Surface.zig
+++ b/src/Surface.zig
@@ -1134,6 +1134,9 @@ pub fn handleMessage(self: *Surface, msg: Message) !void {
 
         .set_mouse_shape => |shape| {
             log.debug("changing mouse shape: {}", .{shape});
+            // hottyterm: over a surface the pointer is its document's; the
+            // program's shows when the pointer leaves it.
+            if (hotty.surfaceHovered(self)) return;
             _ = try self.rt_app.performAction(
                 .{ .surface = self },
                 .mouse_shape,
diff --git a/src/termio/hotty.zig b/src/termio/hotty.zig
index 78b009b27..4723b9c44 100644
--- a/src/termio/hotty.zig
+++ b/src/termio/hotty.zig
@@ -2637,6 +2637,17 @@ fn sameCell(s: *Surface, a: apprt.CursorPos, b: apprt.CursorPos) bool {
     return @floor(ta.x / w) == @floor(tb.x / w) and @floor(ta.y / h) == @floor(tb.y / h);
 }
 
+/// Surface.handleMessage, for the program's pointer shape (OSC 22): whether
+/// a surface is hovered. Its document's shape is then shown (SPEC §9), and
+/// the program's, kept in terminal.mouse_shape, is shown when the pointer
+/// leaves the surface (`shapeChange`). The program sees no motion over a
+/// surface, so the shape it sends then is for where it saw the pointer last.
+pub fn surfaceHovered(s: *Surface) bool {
+    lockState(s, @src());
+    defer s.renderer_state.mutex.unlock(global.io());
+    return s.io.terminal_stream.handler.hotty.hover_len > 0;
+}
+
 /// Shows the pointer's shape and the link preview that changed.
 fn apply(s: *Surface, shape: ?terminal.MouseShape, preview: ?[:0]const u8) void {
     // The pointer shows what the surface under it asks for (SPEC §9).
